The Vulkan backend presents its swap chains through functions the host sets (bgfx::setVkPresentHooks) instead of
vkQueuePresentKHR: the engine presents with Android Frame Pacing (SwappyVk_queuePresent, src/shim/frame_pacing.cpp,
which declares the same struct and function), which times each present to the display's vsync, as the EGL backend
does through bgfx-swap-present-hook.patch. SwappyVk keeps state per swap chain, so the host is also told when one
was created and when it is about to go. VK_GOOGLE_display_timing, the device extension SwappyVk asks for
(SwappyVk_determineDeviceExtensions), joins bgfx's optional extensions on Android. Without hooks set, bgfx presents
with vkQueuePresentKHR. Upstream bgfx has no present hook; keep the patch until it does.

diff --git a/src/renderer_vk.cpp b/src/renderer_vk.cpp
index ff0a16d..84a8bb6 100644
